	"description": [
		"This Business capstone culminates students’ business, liberal arts, co-curricular, and experiential learning. Through applied team projects, practitioner engagement, skill development, and reflection, students synthesize prior experiences; examine how their strengths, values, character, and leadership capacities shape vocational direction; and develop evidence of learning through project work, professional materials, and a portfolio. The course concludes with a presentation, professional narrative, and next-step plan. Offered annually during January term. Prerequisites: BUS 110, BUS 225, and BUS 251 or by permission of the instructor."
